{
 "contract": "uct.converse-eval.cases/1",
 "_": "THE DOOR ACCEPTS WHAT THE BROWSER REFUSES, as cases (Studio, 2026-11-17, Indicators backlog 59). Each case is one request with TWO scripted answers: first the answer the assistant really gave on production, which the door used to accept and the browser then refused whole (a member read \"Nothing was changed\"); then the repaired answer. With the door's rule in place the first is refused at the door, the repair is accepted, the browser applies it and the outputs compute: two model calls, a built indicator. With the rule gone the door accepts the first, the browser refuses it, and the runner fails the case as ACCEPT-THEN-REFUSE. The five rules: colour states on an output drawn as markers; a calculation timeframe on an indicator that draws a marker; the column limit with hidden colour columns counted; a table cell pointing at a setting; a calculation timeframe on an indicator that reads another symbol (graded on the door and the browser's apply alone: there are no second symbol's bars to compute on). ONE MORE CASE is not a door rule (`browser-sends-its-refusal-back`): the door accepts a candle colour that follows a number, the browser refuses it, and the browser sends its own refusal back to the door for one repair. Controls are the standard ones.",
